  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hi Hi! I haven't seen anybody from my point of view report this bug so I'm gonna report it myself!\nThis bug happens when while loading into a world, any world regardless of the file size, sends you back home midway though loading, at random times and points. Sometimes its instant, sometimes its nearly loaded then it sends you back home. Its made going into any world that's over 120MB very annoying. Sometimes I have to join off a friend 3+ times to finally make it in, and it also made world hopping much more tedious.\nThis is mainly a PC issue I believe, however it isn't just a Steam issue, my friend LegendsVR uses a Oculus Quest Link Cable to play and he has this bug pop up just as often as me. I would really want to see this get fixed, as this bug has made certain events and general enjoyment of exploring worlds not as fun anymore.\nI hope to see this get fixed or at least addressed! Thank you for reading!",
